From f08302a5ea02d886c5c004805e6c266692195c3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:23:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] klz: KLZH2, a second entropy stage for the KLZH parse
 (algo only, not yet a codec)

One token per sequence (offset code x min(literal length, 3)), literal-length codes only
from 3, match-length codes in two streams (after a repeat offset / after a new offset), and
every stream cut into khuf chunks where the input crosses a 64 KiB grid, neighbours joined
while one table is estimated to cost no more than two (integer cost estimate). Codec 29's
code path and bytes are unchanged (the parse call moved into kzh_parse). natbench: k2h1..k2h9.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUEN4aRWhUw7yL7cZMqTmZ
